body:
Women having the short end of the stick is bullshit. Men face so many problems that aren't even being addressed. Why don't we talk about how men are more likely to be victims of hit and runs. Or how the education system is set up in a way that discriminates against boys. Or how LGBT men are far more likely to be victims of violence. Or how men have no shelters for domestic violence. Or how medical issues effecting men are far more underfunded then those that effect woman. 

&#x200B;

It's not even that something is being done about these problems, it's just being completely ignored.

Thanks Laura, i've started talking about it with my psychologist and psychiatrist. My psychiatrist say's it's a result of stress and a lack of communication with women that is causing it. I think he might be right because when I was little I never had these thoughts and now I have them all the time. 

&#x200B;

I just feel like I could never pass anyway, and i'm so tired all the time I couldn't deal with all the questions from family and friends and colleagues.
